arks contributors"],"artisticLicense":"CC-BY-4.0","spatialDataLicense":"ODbL-1.0","licenseScope":"CC BY applies to original artistic contributions only; ODbL applies to OSM-derived spatial data. Reference photographs retain their own licenses.","review":{"status":"pending","reviewer":null,"checks":{}},"modelingNotes":["This asset is the northern Philippe Auguste column, not both Trone columns or the adjacent pavilion. The chosen OSM way has a cruciform 4 m pedestal, small central 4.5 m parts and a 28 m overall height, but no mapped upper shaft.","The inspected Philippe Auguste column photograph establishes the slender fluted shaft, broad capital and green standing figure. The two small mapped central parts straddle the axis; their union and the outline set the centered shaft and a solid connecting plinth. Elevations 4.5–24 m for the shaft, 24–25.1 m for the capital and 28 m overall are explicit proportional inferences constrained by OSM total height.","The finial is an original abstract standing silhouette, not a reproduction of the statue. Fluting, reliefs, coats of arms, lettering and capital carving are omitted. Nearby gate pavilion and southern Saint-Louis column are outside this footprint."],"source":{"url":"/objects/1fe5c90950e2789c86456736bf17017a07482fcde0aa5032cfaf867943484cce/source.blend.gz","bytes":115003,"sha256":"1fe5c90950e2789c86456736bf17017a07482fcde0aa5032cfaf867943484cce"},"spatialSource":{"url":"/objects/f00e923dd5c4031b50e13800ae9fe4b8921ecbd4c960ba5348402aece1db4817/spatial-source.json","bytes":4813,"sha256":"f00e923dd5c4031b50e13800ae9fe4b8921ecbd4c960ba5348402aece1db4817"},"preview":{"url":"/objects/b90acc61cdfa303dfec5d78911c28e0f4b08868bb4d8c1c13ec5cb9a05509dbf/preview.webp","bytes":4128,"sha256":"b90acc61cdfa303dfec5d78911c28e0f4b08868bb4d8c1c13ec5cb9a05509dbf"},"revision":"41ab075fc199b3073d80a6fd3f8876d9909f7f104aa4ba4344840d36c5f79293","publicationRevision":"6bb5a372d91c61e176af13c7f0522c37acd3f1aa19be403f9a91df233bbe44bc","bounds":[2.